\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Protocol evolution across rounds on the nine long-horizon and production-oriented benchmarks, which form the rows. Solid ovals are agent roles, small pills inside a dashed container are internal phases of a single-agent solver, solid edges are admissible handoffs, and dashed edges are validity or retry edges. A panel shows everything the protocol carries at that round, where boxed text pinned to an element is a transition or completion predicate and the lower container holds the shared rule and culture. Elements introduced by the current round are drawn in the color of their edit level from Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:self_evolving}, and elements carried from an earlier round are drawn in gray, so a round that leaves the graph unchanged still shows what it revised.}}{17}{figure.46}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:case_evo}{{7}{17}{Protocol evolution across rounds on the nine long-horizon and production-oriented benchmarks, which form the rows. Solid ovals are agent roles, small pills inside a dashed container are internal phases of a single-agent solver, solid edges are admissible handoffs, and dashed edges are validity or retry edges. A panel shows everything the protocol carries at that round, where boxed text pinned to an element is a transition or completion predicate and the lower container holds the shared rule and culture. Elements introduced by the current round are drawn in the color of their edit level from Section~\ref {sec:self_evolving}, and elements carried from an earlier round are drawn in gray, so a round that leaves the graph unchanged still shows what it revised}{figure.46}{}}
